WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:04.301
A flying car is not just a car with an extra engine.

2
00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:10.251
Every gram matters. Every component changes the balance of the entire system.

3
00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:15.526
We can explore the visible machine and use engineering-informed reconstructions to

4
00:00:15.576 --> 00:00:17.237
understand the ideas.

5
00:00:17.652 --> 00:00:23.202
Importantly, Tesla has not published complete internal mechanical drawings.

6
00:00:23.277 --> 00:00:29.287
The system shown here is an educational concept, not a leaked production design.

7
00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:35.024
A road car is optimized for tire contact, passenger comfort and crash safety.

8
00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:41.616
An aircraft must also accommodate lift-producing systems, a stable center of mass,

9
00:00:41.716 --> 00:00:45.316
flight controls and redundant safety provisions.

10
00:00:45.596 --> 00:00:51.346
Packing both missions into one body turns each design choice into a tradeoff.

11
00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:57.195
The Roadster exterior gives visual clues about its low roofline, cabin and wheelbase.

12
00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:03.674
It does not tell us the precise configuration of unpublished internal hardware.

13
00:01:03.699 --> 00:01:10.349
In our reconstruction, fans, gas storage and electronics are labeled concepts: they

14
00:01:10.424 --> 00:01:15.349
demonstrate physical principles without implying we possess Tesla engineering

15
00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:16.093
drawings.

16
00:01:16.584 --> 00:01:21.934
Select a subsystem and watch it leave the vehicle into an inspection position.

17
00:01:22.034 --> 00:01:26.909
Look for the forces entering its structure and the interfaces it must share with its

18
00:01:26.984 --> 00:01:31.984
neighbors. The physical challenge is never just the part by itself.

19
00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:36.155
It is how a complete vehicle behaves when everything is integrated.
